---
import DesignSystemShell from "../../layouts/DesignSystemShell.astro";
import DsSection from "../../components/design-system/DsSection.astro";
import DsRule from "../../components/design-system/DsRule.astro";
import DsSpec from "../../components/design-system/DsSpec.astro";
import DsToken from "../../components/design-system/DsToken.astro";
import { token, tokensIn } from "@lib/design-system/tokens";

const spaces = tokensIn("space");
const radii = tokensIn("radius");
const container = token("--container")?.resolved;
const gutter = token("--gutter")?.resolved;

const spaceUse: Record<string, string> = {
  "--space-1": "Hairline gaps: nav link gap, chip inner gap, dept-items gap (2px is the one sub-token exception)",
  "--space-2": "Tight inline gaps: pill rows, button groups, chip rows, KPI grid gap on cash surfaces (7px rounds to this)",
  "--space-3": "Control padding, toolbar gap (10px rounds to this), nav-bar block padding",
  "--space-4": "In-card gaps, between stacked cards, board grid gap (14px rounds to this), card padding on dense boards",
  "--space-5": "Specimen and popup padding",
  "--space-6": "Card padding, default block spacing, rail padding",
  "--space-8": "Generous internal spacing; page body padding on the design-system site; main horizontal padding is 28px (the recorded full-bleed constant)",
  "--space-10": "Band separation (masthead / nav to content)",
  "--space-12": "Large block padding",
  "--space-16": "Section-to-section rhythm on public pages",
};

const radiusUse: Record<string, string> = {
  "--radius-sm": "Segments inside a segmented control; toolbar inputs on the shell; small chips",
  "--radius-md": "Default — buttons, cards, inputs, tiles, chip on the rail (6px is the one recorded exception)",
  "--radius-lg": "Larger documentation cards; board groups and cash-map cells use 10px, popups 10px",
  "--radius-xl": "Reserved for oversized containers; audit KPI cards use 14px on the boards",
  "--radius-full": "Pills, dots, meter tracks, badge discs",
};
---

<DesignSystemShell slug="spacing" source="app/command-center/src/styles/global.css">
  <DsSection id="scale" title="Spacing scale">
    <p>
      Every margin, padding and gap is a token on a 4px base, named by its multiple of 4. The scale is deliberately sparse
      above 24px — large spacing wants a few decisive choices, not a continuum. Where a shipped surface uses an
      off-scale value (7px, 10px, 14px, 18px, 28px on the boards) it is recorded beside the nearest token; new work
      snaps to the token.
    </p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th class="num">px</th><th>Bar</th><th>Common use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {spaces.map((s) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nowrap"><DsToken name={s.name} /></td>
              <td class="num">{s.resolved}</td>
              <td><span style={`display:block;height:10px;width:${s.resolved};background:var(--info);border-radius:2px`}></span></td>
              <td>{spaceUse[s.name]}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>Radius</h3>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th class="num">Value</th><th>Specimen</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {radii.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nowrap"><DsToken name={r.name} /></td>
              <td class="num">{r.resolved}</td>
              <td><span style={`display:inline-block;width:44px;height:28px;border:1px solid var(--border-strong);background:var(--surface-alt);border-radius:${r.resolved}`}></span></td>
              <td>{radiusUse[r.name]}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Radii within one visual group are uniform (DSN-015): a card group does not mix <code>xl</code> and <code>sm</code>. The board convention is 14px top-level card, 10–11px nested row, 8px input, 999px pill.</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="app-frame" title="App frame">
    <p>The Command Center is a fixed-rail application shell. Structural rails are fixed by intent; content within them is fluid.</p>
    <DsSpec label="Frame anatomy at 1440 × 900" layout="block">
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:140px 1fr;gap:0;border:1px solid var(--border-strong);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;font-size:11px">
        <div style="background:var(--primary);color:#fff;padding:12px;display:grid;gap:8px;align-content:start">
          <div style="background:#fff;border-radius:4px;height:26px"></div>
          <div style="height:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.25);border-radius:3px;width:70%"></div>
          <div style="height:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.15);border-radius:3px"></div>
          <div style="height:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.15);border-radius:3px"></div>
          <div style="height:10px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.15);border-radius:3px"></div>
          <div style="margin-top:auto;color:rgba(255,255,255,.7)">rail · 280px</div>
        </div>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-rows:auto 1fr;background:var(--surface-inset)">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:12px 14px 8px;background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><span>top bar · 24px 28px 16px</span><span style="color:var(--text-muted)">operator cluster</span></div>
          <div style="padding:16px 28px 24px;display:grid;gap:8px;align-content:start"><div style="border:1px dashed var(--border-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;color:var(--text-muted)">main · padding 16px 28px 24px · min-width 0</div><div style="border:1px dashed var(--border-strong);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;color:var(--text-muted)">a full-bleed board bleeds by exactly −28px horizontally (S-05)</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </DsSpec>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Size</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Side rail</td><td>280px (240px ≤ 1180px; hidden ≤ 820px or when collapsed)</td><td>Fixed. Navy, padding 24px 18px, gap 24px between blocks. Collapse persists in <code>cc-rail-collapsed</code> and is restored before first paint.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Top bar</td><td>auto height; padding 24px 28px 16px</td><td>Rail toggle 34×34 · eyebrow + h1 · runtime pill + version · operator card (min 168px) · sign out. No breadcrumbs: eyebrow + title carry hierarchy.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Main</td><td>1fr, <code>min-width: 0</code></td><td><code>min-width: 0</code> is what lets a wide table scroll inside instead of widening the page.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Main padding</td><td>16px 28px 24px</td><td>The 28px is a recorded constant: full-bleed boards negate exactly this much (client report 2026-06-28).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Design-system rail</td><td>272px (240px ≤ 1180px)</td><td>Same navy, same 36px link height; chapter nav instead of departments.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="container" title="The content rail">
    <p>Reading surfaces (public pages, documentation, department overviews) use one content rail. Full-bleed regions put their background on the band and their content inside the rail, so every edge lines up without per-element matching.</p>
    <div class="ds-pre"><code>.container &#123;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: var(--container);   /* {container} — caps the measure */
  margin-inline: auto;           /* centres it */
  padding-inline: var(--gutter); /* {gutter} — fluid side space */
&#125;</code></div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Why hybrid:</strong> pure % gives 2000px lines on a wide monitor; pure fixed is cramped at 380px. <code>max-width</code> caps, <code>clamp()</code> gutters flex.</li>
      <li><strong>Per-context exception:</strong> application chrome (the rail) stays fixed. Fluid-vs-fixed is chosen per context, never blanket.</li>
      <li><strong>There is never a second container definition.</strong> A 24px stagger between two bands is always a second definition of "the column"; delete it, do not nudge it.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="breakpoints" title="Breakpoints">
    <p>Four breakpoints, all <code>max-width</code>, all in the shell or in the surface that needs them. Coverage is deliberately thin: the Command Center is a desktop work surface, and the mobile-first companion (CRM PWA) is a separate app with this system's tokens. Every breakpoint's behaviour is in <a href="/design-system/mobile#breakpoint-behaviour">Mobile</a>.</p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th class="num">Width</th><th>Name</th><th>What changes</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 1280px</td><td>toc</td><td>The design-system's right-hand "On this page" list hides</td><td>design-system.css</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 1180px</td><td>rail</td><td>Rail 280 → 240; 4-up metric grids → 2-up; two-column workbenches → 1; sticky detail panels → static; executive KPIs 4 → 3</td><td>global.css</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 1100px</td><td>board</td><td>Board KPI grids 4 → 2 (Invoice Audit, Order Audit, Agreement Builder, Credit Memos)</td><td>per-surface CSS</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 980px</td><td>—</td><td>Operator cluster wraps</td><td>global.css</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 900px</td><td>—</td><td>Runtime board stacks</td><td>agents.astro</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">≤ 820px</td><td>stack</td><td>Rail hides (frame becomes one column); heading rows stack; action rows go full width; executive KPIs → 2 and account bars wrap</td><td>global.css</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">320px</td><td>floor</td><td><code>html &#123; min-width: 320px &#125;</code> — nothing narrower is supported</td><td>global.css</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="full-bleed" title="Full-bleed work surfaces">
    <p>
      Boards (Friday WIP/AR, Invoice Audit, the cash family, Order/Estimate Audit, Agreement Builder) fill the main column
      edge to edge so their own background reads as the room the work happens in. The contract is exact, because getting it
      wrong pushes the panel under the rail (as it did on 2026-06-28).
    </p>
    <div class="ds-pre"><code>.fw &#123;
  margin: calc(-1 * var(--space-4)) -28px calc(-1 * var(--space-6));  /* negate main's padding exactly */
  padding: 18px 28px 30px;                                             /* re-pad by the same amount */
  min-height: 70vh;
  overflow-x: clip;        /* the board never scrolls the page sideways; its .fw-tablewrap scrolls */
  display: grid; gap: 14px;
&#125;</code></div>
    <ul>
      <li>Horizontal bleed equals main's horizontal padding (28px). Not more, not less.</li>
      <li><code>overflow-x: clip</code> on the root; <code>overflow: auto</code> on each table wrapper (never <code>overflow-y: visible</code> paired with <code>overflow-x: auto</code>).</li>
      <li>The board's toolbar is the first child; its title is an <code>h2</code> at 18px, not a second page title.</li>
      <li>Rail collapse exists for boards: a wide board is the reason the toggle was built.</li>
    </ul>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="density" title="Density">
    <p>Two densities, chosen by the job. A surface is one or the other; it does not mix them.</p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Reading (shell, overviews, this site)</th><th>Working (boards, audit trees)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Body size</td><td>14px / 1.5</td><td>12.5–13px / 1.45</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Table row height</td><td>~46px (13px 14px cell padding)</td><td>29px (4px 8px cell padding) — WIP went from 67px to 29px rows and 3 → 11 visible rows at 1920×900</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Card padding</td><td>16–24px</td><td>7–14px</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Grid gap</td><td>16–24px</td><td>7–14px</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Control height</td><td>44px buttons, 38px inputs</td><td>32–38px controls; 30px small buttons</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Touch target</td><td>44px min</td><td>36px min on desktop-only boards; 44px if the board is ever used on a tablet</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Headers</td><td>12px caps, 0 tracking</td><td>10–11px caps, 0.03–0.04em</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Radius</td><td>8px</td><td>14 / 10 / 8 / 999</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="z-index" title="Stacking order">
    <p>Six layers. A new element joins a layer; it does not invent a number.</p>
    <div class="ds-table-wrap">
      <table class="ds-table">
        <thead><tr><th class="num">z</th><th>Layer</th><th>Members</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="num">1</td><td>Sticky table header</td><td>Board <code>thead th</code> (3 on frozen tables), spec-table headers</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">2</td><td>Frozen column</td><td>First-column cells on frozen boards (header corner cell is 4)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">20</td><td>Toolbar dropdowns & sticky top bar</td><td><code>.iv-more-body</code>, the design-system top bar</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">30</td><td>Map controls & legend</td><td>Territory Map overlays</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">40</td><td>Popouts</td><td>The one shared popout node (WIP "best guess"), InfoWindow cards</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="num">50</td><td>Toast</td><td>Single fixed bottom-centre node, <code>role="status"</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Recorded failure this prevents: the CRM companion's WIP sub-bar (z-40) covered its primary nav (z-30). A sub-bar is layer 20 at most.</p>
  </DsSection>

  <DsSection id="spacing-rules" title="Rules">
    <div class="ds-rules">
      <DsRule id="S-01" title="Every gap is a --space-* token; no raw pixel margins or paddings in component CSS." source="Design.md 'Layout & spacing'; DSN-014">
        <p>Existing off-scale board values (7, 10, 14, 18px) are recorded, not precedent. New boards use 8 / 12 / 16 / 20.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-02" title="Reading surfaces align to one .container; structural rails are fixed." source="Design.md 'The container'">
        <p>Background on the band, content in the container. Never a negative-margin hack to fake full-bleed on a reading page.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-03" title="Radius is 8px by default; pills are full; one radius per visual group." source="Design.md 'Shape'; DSN-015">
        <p>Boards: 14 top-level, 10 nested, 8 inputs, 999 pills.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-04" title="Density is chosen per surface — reading or working — and never mixed within one." source="docs/40 §2; WIP density rework 2026-08-21">
        <p>A board that needs a paragraph puts it in a note at 12.5px, not a 14px block.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-05" title="A full-bleed board negates main's padding by exactly 28px horizontally and re-pads the same amount." source="invoice-audit.astro:202-205 (client report 2026-06-28)">
        <p>Bleeding more pushed the panel under the rail and past the right edge.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-06" title="Main has min-width: 0 and a wide table scrolls its own wrapper, never the page." source="global.css .app-main; invoice-audit.astro:209, :343">
        <p><code>overflow-x: clip</code> on the surface root, <code>overflow: auto</code> on the table wrap.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-07" title="Breakpoints are 1280 / 1180 / 1100 / 820 and the 320 floor; a new one needs a recorded reason." source="global.css media queries; this chapter">
        <p>Prefer <code>auto-fit, minmax()</code> grids that need no breakpoint at all.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-08" title="Stacking uses the six recorded layers; a sub-bar never outranks navigation." source="this chapter; CRM parity review P0 2026-09-11">
        <p>Toast is the only element above a popout.</p>
      </DsRule>
      <DsRule id="S-09" title="Sticky offsets and pane heights are measured from the rendered DOM, never hardcoded." source="standards/design/v1.md § Long-list disclosure">
        <p>A 5px-short offset is a 5px band of body rows above the header.</p>
      </DsRule>
    </div>
  </DsSection>
</DesignSystemShell>
